messages:
maya: Heads-up: building a Next.js starter for the DX repo (edge runtime + TS + LangChain) — running into auth + retry weirdness with the SDK in browser context. First request returns 401, SDK retries 3x and essentially DDoSes our auth endpoint. Anyone seen this? :thinking_face:

alex: Are you using cookie-based auth or ephemeral tokens? Edge runtime can behave differently with cookies (SameSite/secure). Also FYI we had a fix for fetch credentials in a recent PR — can you paste the minimal error?

maya: Console error (browser):

```
FetchError: request to https://auth.internal.redwood.example/session failed, status code 401
    at fetch.then.res (sdk/request.js:142:22)
    at processTicksAndRejections (internal/process/task_queues.js:93:5)
```

maya: After that the SDK retries x3 and then the login flow kicks in. Repro is simple: Next.js + app route calling SDK from client (edge runtime).

sam: I reproduced locally using `export const runtime = 'edge'` in app/route and got the same behavior. Looks like our retry wrapper treats 401 as transient in the edge fetch shim. Filed a repro and minimal steps: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/issues/789 — includes a tiny Next app that fails. :bug:

jim: There's an older example that uses server components (not edge) at https://github.com/redwood-inference/examples/tree/main/next-langchain-starter — compare server vs edge behavior. Temporary workaround: set env REDWOOD_SDK_RETRIES=0 for the client build so it doesn't retry on auth errors.

dev-bot: CI alert — examples/next-edge-starter tests failed on commit 32a5c2 (auth-flow.spec.ts flaked). Logs: https://ci.redwood.com/builds/123456

alex: Short-term plan: add a runtime-aware default in the SDK and expose a config flag `retryOnAuthError: false`. I'll open a PR to the SDK and add a dedicated example in examples/next-edge-starter showing correct client-side usage. cc @sdk-team

sdk-team: Triaged. Plan: 1) runtime detection (edge vs node) in the HTTP client, 2) expose retry config with env override, 3) update Quickstart and Next starter docs. ETA ~3 days.

maya: Thanks — I'll try the REDWOOD_SDK_RETRIES=0 workaround and link the GH issue in the starter README. If someone can paste a minimal snippet for client-side fetch (cookies + edge) that'd be super helpful.

alex: Snippet — client call from app/page.tsx with cookie-include pattern: 

```ts
// app/actions/sendPrompt.ts (edge client call)
export const runtime = 'edge';
import { initRedwood } from 'redwood-sdk';

const client = initRedwood({ baseUrl: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_REDWOOD_API });

export async function sendPrompt(prompt: string) {
  const res = await fetch(`${client.baseUrl}/v1/generate`, {
    method: 'POST',
    credentials: 'include', // important for cookies in edge
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ prompt }),
  });
  if (res.status === 401) return { ok: false, unauth: true };
  return res.json();
}
```

alex: The key is credentials: 'include' and short-circuiting 401 so the SDK doesn't treat it as transient. We'll add a helper `client.setRetryPolicy({ retryOnAuthError: false })`.

maya: Tested the snippet with the env workaround — retries stopped, still getting 401 (expected), so I can wire the redirect client-side. Filed internal ticket: https://redwood.atlassian.net/browse/DEVEX-291 to track adding the example + doc updates.

sam: :thumbsup: I'll attach the failing repro to DEVEX-291 and add the flaky CI logs.

maya: Appreciate the quick triage — ping me once the PR lands and I'll update the starter template in the DX repo.
